IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc5-logic`
IMPORT `ssc5-part6`

-- Tests for ssc5-part6.l4 (ss 112 to 122).  Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- section named beside it, before the run.
-- Day-of-week anchors: 1 December 2025 was a Monday, so 30 November 2025 was a Sunday.

§ `Tests -- Part VI`

§§ `s 112 -- employment protection entitlement`

#ASSERT `s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` `s 112(3)(b) a sum payable by way of pay in pursuance of an order under that Act or the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 for the continuation of a contract of employment` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` `s 112(3)(c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` `s 112(3) some other sum` EQUALS FALSE

-- Arguments: the sum; only a part of it is in question; that part is prescribed; a prescribed amount treated as related.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(b) a sum payable by way of pay in pursuance of an order under that Act or the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 for the continuation of a contract of employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A part of a mentioned sum counts only if prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Prescribed amounts that regulations treat as related to those sums.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3) some other sum` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither limb: "means" closes the definition.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3) some other sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `s 112(3) some other sum` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 113(1) -- disqualification`

-- Arguments: a benefit under Parts II to V; absent from Great Britain; in legal custody; regulations otherwise provide.
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither absent nor in custody: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a benefit under Parts II to V.
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Except where regulations otherwise provide": points outside the text.
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 115 and 116 -- Crown employment and the forces`

-- (1) and (2). Arguments: employed by or under the Crown; serving as a member of the forces in that capacity.
#ASSERT `s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: as a member of the forces; other prescribed employment under the Crown.
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 116(1). Arguments: serving; the purpose.
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of this Part of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(b) a purpose of a provision of the Administration Act in its application to him as an employed earner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Subject to s 115(3): not for Part V.
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` TRUE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Part V of this Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` TRUE `s 116(1) some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not serving: "while he is so serving".
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` FALSE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` FALSE `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Part V of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 116(3). Arguments: prescribed; persons serve in it under the control of the Defence Council.
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the establishment or organisation is part of Her Majesty's forces` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the establishment or organisation is part of Her Majesty's forces` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the establishment or organisation is part of Her Majesty's forces` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the establishment or organisation is part of Her Majesty's forces` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 117, 119, 120 -- the exceptions to s 94(5)`

#ASSERT `s 117 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 117 the accident falls within the exception` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 117 the accident falls within the exception` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 119 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 119 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 119 the accident falls within the exception` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Arguments: continental shelf operations; prescribed employment; regulations under s 120(1) apply the provision.
#ASSERT `s 120 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 120 the accident falls within the exception` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 120 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 120 the accident falls within the exception` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 122(1) -- deferred`

-- Arguments: the kind of pension; the answer of s 55(3); the answer of s 55C(3).
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a Category A or Category B retirement pension` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a Category A or Category B retirement pension` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a Category A or Category B retirement pension` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a shared additional pension` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a shared additional pension` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) a shared additional pension` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the pension is deferred` `s 122(1) some other pension` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 122(1) -- tax year`

-- A tax year begins on 6 April and is named by the calendar year in which it begins.
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 5 4 2024))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2023
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 6 4 2024))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 31 12 2024))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 1 1 2025))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 5 4 2025))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` (Date 6 4 2025))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2025

-- "1978-79" is the tax year beginning with 6 April 1978.
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` 1978 1979 EQUALS JUST (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 1978)
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` 1999 2000 EQUALS JUST (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 1999)
-- Not successive years.
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` 1978 1980 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` 1978 1978 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` 1979 1978 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 122(1) -- tax week`

-- The tax year 2024-25 runs 6 April 2024 to 5 April 2025 (365 days): weeks 1 to 52 of seven days each, and the
-- last day is a separate tax week, the 53rd.
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 6 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 12 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 13 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 28 3 2025))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 51
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 29 3 2025))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 52
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 4 4 2025))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 52
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 5 4 2025))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 53
#ASSERT ((`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 5 4 2025))'s `the tax year`)'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2024
-- 2023-24 ends in a leap year: 6 April 2023 to 5 April 2024 is 366 days, and the last two days are one tax week.
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 6 4 2023))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 3 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 52
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 4 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 53
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 5 4 2024))'s `number of the week in the year` EQUALS 53
#ASSERT ((`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` (Date 5 4 2024))'s `the tax year`)'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2023

§§ `s 122(1) -- week, and qualifying earnings factor`

-- "week" is a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday.
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 30 11 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 30 11 2025))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 6 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 3 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 6 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 7 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 7 12 2025))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 13 12 2025
-- Across a year end: Thursday 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 1 2026))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 28 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 1 2026))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 3 1 2026

-- "the lower earnings limit for the tax year in question multiplied by 52".  The limit is an input, so the
-- figures here are arbitrary.
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the qualifying earnings factor in pounds` (`Earnings limits` WITH `the tax year` IS (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 2024), `lower earnings limit` IS 100, `primary threshold` IS 200, `upper earnings limit` IS 900, `secondary threshold` IS 150) EQUALS 5200
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the qualifying earnings factor in pounds` (`Earnings limits` WITH `the tax year` IS (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS 2024), `lower earnings limit` IS 123.5, `primary threshold` IS 200, `upper earnings limit` IS 900, `secondary threshold` IS 150) EQUALS 6422

§§ `s 122(1) -- the records of how a term is defined`

#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional Class 4 percentage`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional Class 4 percentage`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 15(3ZA)(b) above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) beneficiary`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) beneficiary`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the person entitled to that benefit"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) employment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "includes"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the benefits code`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) child`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the same meaning as in Part 9 of this Act (section 142(1))"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) prescribe`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "prescribe by regulations"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) ITEPA 2003`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) late husband`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "in relation to a woman who has been more than once married, her last husband"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) working life`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) relative`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "includes"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) loss of physical faculty`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "includes"`

§§ `s 122(4) to (6B)`

-- (4) Arguments: residing with his spouse; the answer of s 141 for the spouse.
#ASSERT `s 122(4) the person is treated as entitled to the child benefit to which the spouse is entitled` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(4) the person is treated as entitled to the child benefit to which the spouse is entitled` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(4) the person is treated as entitled to the child benefit to which the spouse is entitled` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(4) the person is treated as entitled to the child benefit to which the spouse is entitled` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6) "if (but only if)" both limbs hold.
#ASSERT `s 122(6) the person is permanently incapable of self-support` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(6) the person is permanently incapable of self-support` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 122(6) the person is permanently incapable of self-support` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 122(6) the person is permanently incapable of self-support` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (6B) Arguments: the amount prescribed; the arithmetical equivalent.  "exceeds by not more than 1 pound".
#ASSERT `s 122(6B) the amount prescribed is one the power includes` 10.5 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(6B) the amount prescribed is one the power includes` 11 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(6B) the amount prescribed is one the power includes` 11.01 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(6B) the amount prescribed is one the power includes` 10 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 122(6B) the amount prescribed is one the power includes` 9 10 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 122(1) -- unless the context otherwise requires`

#ASSERT `s 122(1) the defined meaning applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 122(1) the defined meaning applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 122(1) -- one test for each record of a defined term`

-- For each of the 62 records: the way the Act defines the term (decided by reading the cited lines: "means", "includes",
-- "to be construed in accordance with", "has the meaning given by", another Act's meaning), then what it points at or says.
-- The first assertion of each pair was checked against the cited lines by a keyword classification of the raw text
-- (two lines it could not read, "period of deferment" and "general earnings", were read by hand); the second repeats the
-- record's words and is a guard against a record being re-pointed, not an independent check of the wording.

#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional Class 4 percentage`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional Class 4 percentage`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 15(3ZA)(b) above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional primary percentage`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) additional primary percentage`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 8(2)(b) above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) adult disability payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) adult disability payment`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) age-related secondary percentage`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) age-related secondary percentage`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 9A(2) above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) Bank of England base rate`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) Bank of England base rate`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the rate announced from time to time by the Monetary Policy Committee of the Bank of England as the official dealing rate, or, where an order under section 19 of the Bank of England Act 1998 is in force, any equivalent rate determined by the Treasury under that section"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) beneficiary`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) beneficiary`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the person entitled to that benefit"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) benefit`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) benefit`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "benefit under Parts II to V of this Act other than Old Cases payments; as respects any period before 1st July 1992 but not before 6th April 1975, benefit under Part II of the 1975 Act; or as respects any period before 6th April 1975, benefit under the National Insurance Act 1946 or 1965 or the National Insurance (Industrial Injuries) Act 1946 or 1965"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the benefits code`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the benefits code`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the meaning given by section 63(1) of ITEPA 2003"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) child`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) child`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the same meaning as in Part 9 of this Act (section 142(1))"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) child disability payment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) child disability payment`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 (S.S.I. 2021/174)"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claim`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claim`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "claimant"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claimant, other than for industrial injuries benefit`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claimant, other than for industrial injuries benefit`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "a person who has claimed benefit"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claimant, for industrial injuries benefit`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) claimant, for industrial injuries benefit`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "a person who has claimed industrial injuries benefit"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) contract of service`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) contract of service`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "any contract of service or apprenticeship whether written or oral and whether express or implied"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) contribution-based jobseeker's allowance`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) contribution-based jobseeker's allowance`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the same meaning as in the Jobseekers Act 1995"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) current`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) current`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "for the time being in force (of the lower and upper earnings limits and primary and secondary thresholds under section 5(1) above)"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) day of interruption of employment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) day of interruption of employment`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 25A(1)(c) above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) period of deferment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) period of deferment`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "for a Category A or Category B retirement pension, section 55(3); for a shared additional pension, section 55C(3)"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) earner and earnings`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) earner and earnings`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "sections 3, 4 and 112 above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) employed earner`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) employed earner`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "section 2 above"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) employment`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "includes"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) employment`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "any trade, business, profession, office or vocation, and employed has a corresponding meaning"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the employment income Parts of ITEPA 2003`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "Parts 2 to 7A of that Act"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) entitled`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) entitled`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the provisions specifically relating to that benefit; for a benefit specified in section 20(1) above, section 21 above; and sections 1 to 3 of the Administration Act and section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) first appointed year and second appointed year`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) first appointed year and second appointed year`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "such tax year, no earlier than 2002-03, as may be appointed by order, and such subsequent tax year as may be so appointed"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the flat rate introduction year`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) the flat rate introduction year`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "such tax year as may be designated as such by order"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) general earnings`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) general earnings`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "the meaning given by section 7 of ITEPA 2003, and accordingly sections 3 and 112 of this Act do not apply to the word earnings in the expression general earnings"
#ASSERT (`s 122(1) industrial injuries benefit`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
